From: elliotttate <elliotttate@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 21:21:50 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 136/138] Aurora: the GPU profiler without Tracy
 (DOL_AURORA_GPU_PROF=1)

The timestamp profiler (gpu_prof.cpp) was built only with Tracy. It is
now always built, and DOL_AURORA_GPU_PROF=1 requests the timestamp
feature and writes [gpu-prof] lines to stderr every 240 frames: the
frames' GPU time, the top-level passes' busy time, each pass and zone
kind's time per frame ("Render pass 12" counts as "Render pass"), and
the KB the frame's staging copies move (vertices, uniforms, indices,
storage, textures). Without the variable nothing changes: the feature is
not requested and every pass_writes() is null, as before.
